# Each phrase announces a point instead of making it, so the whole
# list is unconditional. `clearly`, `interestingly`, `importantly`,
# `notably`, and `crucially` count only with a glued comma, the
# sentence-adverb shape (`Clearly, the cache is cold`), because the
# bare adverb modifies a verb (`the error prints clearly`).
expr main [(note that), (it is worth noting), (it's worth noting), (worth noting), (it should be noted), (it must be noted), (please note), (keep in mind), (bear in mind), (it is important to [note, remember, understand, mention, realize, recognize]), (it's important to [note, remember, understand, mention, realize, recognize]), (needless to say), (as you can see), (as mentioned), (as noted), (as stated), (as discussed), (as described [above, earlier, before, previously]), obviously, (of course), (clearly,), (in other words), (to put it simply), (put simply), (simply put), (that is to say), (to be clear), (make no mistake), (it goes without saying), (it is worth mentioning), (it's worth mentioning), (interestingly,), (importantly,), (notably,), (crucially,)]
let message "Throat clearing. Delete the phrase and state the point."
let description "Flags phrases that announce a point instead of making it."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The error prints clearly on a dark background."
allows "The lookup is not an offset into the token list."
allows "The note field holds free text."
